In the early game, mines may not yet have been
found, therefore guaranteed dwarf generation may not
be available, nor the combination of player level
and dungeon level high enough to generate dwarves
with such tools on normal levels. So no, in the
early game, lacking all of such usually-later-on
discovered resources as boots or spells of jumping,
dwarf-dropped (or randomly generated) digging tools,
nor IDed wands of digging, it is unlikely that the
PC will have much choice but starvation if corridor
traps prevent access to the down stairs and thus
safe re-access to the already located up-stairs.

The issue pretty much cures itself by the time the
player reaches XL 7 or so, or DLVL 9 or so, but to
me, traps in corridors pose a severe threat to the
early game chances that the PC will survive.

